---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeTabs from "../../components/CodeTabs.vue";
import "../../styles/global.css";

const tabs = [
  {
    label: "inject (client)",
    code: `/* Push the current span's context into outgoing headers.
   The carrier is yours: two callbacks, no HTTP struct imposed. */
otlp_context_t ctx = otlp_context_from_span(span);

otlp_context_inject(ctx, my_set_header, &request_headers);
/* → traceparent: 00-<32 hex trace>-<16 hex span>-01
   → tracestate:  vendor1=1,vendor2=2   (if set)
   → baggage:     env=prod,tenant=acme  (if set) */`,
  },
  {
    label: "extract (server)",
    code: `/* Reconstruct the parent context on the receiving side.
   Returns has_context=false for an empty/invalid carrier —
   never a garbage context. */
otlp_context_t parent = otlp_context_extract(
    my_get_header, &incoming_headers);

if (parent.has_context) {
    /* start the child span under the caller's trace */
    otlp_span_set_trace_id(child, parent.trace_id);
    otlp_span_set_parent_span_id(child, parent.span_id);
    otlp_span_set_trace_state(child, parent.trace_state);
}`,
  },
  {
    label: "the carrier callbacks",
    code: `/* One setter, one getter — any header store works:
   curl_slist, h2 headers, raw bufs, your RPC metadata. */
static void my_set_header(const char *name, const char *value, void *ud) {
    headers_add(ud, name, value);
}
static const char *my_get_header(const char *name, void *ud) {
    return headers_get(ud, name);   /* NULL when absent */
}`,
  },
];
---
<Docs title="Context propagation — otlp-c docs">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-50">Context propagation</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-slate-400">
    Distributed tracing needs the trace to survive the hop. otlp-c
    implements W3C Trace Context (traceparent + tracestate) and W3C
    Baggage, spec-exact — including the rules most implementations
    get wrong: version <code class="font-mono text-xs text-teal-300">0xff</code>
    rejection, future-version forward compatibility, printable-only
    tracestate/baggage, and big-endian ratio-sampler prefixes.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8">
    <CodeTabs client:load tabs={tabs} />
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100">The guarantees</h2>
  <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60 p-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Spec-exact traceparent</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        Exactly four fields for version 00; all-zero IDs rejected on
        both inject and extract; CR/LF never propagated (the same
        CWE-93 posture as the HTTP layer — injection attempts fail
        closed, they don't launder).
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60 p-5">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Baggage, not a side channel</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        Only printable ASCII propagates; malformed entries are
        dropped, not forwarded. Extract returns
        <code class="font-mono text-xs text-teal-300">has_context=false</code>
        rather than a zero-filled context that would silently break
        correlation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-100">Sampling interacts here</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
    The built-in samplers — always_on, always_off,
    trace_id_ratio_based — decide at span creation from the trace
    id's big-endian prefix, so decisions are consistent across
    processes regardless of endianness. The sampled flag rides the
    last traceparent byte.
  </p>
</Docs>
